<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18373" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flexūra</span></b> , ae, f.
		flexus, from flecto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a bending</i>, <i>winding</i>,
				<i>turning</i> (rare; not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lateris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 336</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">angustiae flexuraeque vicorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 38</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtus recta est: flexuram non recipit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 71, 19</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gram., <i>inflection</i>, <i>declension</i> of a word,
				<i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 10, § 28</span></i>
			Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
